{"t": 1794111284.6806087, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fix/pagination-57", "files": [{"content": "def page(items: list, number: int, size: int) -> list:\n    start = (number - 1) * size\n    return items[start:start + size]\n", "path": "catalog/pager.py"}], "message": "Fix page() to use 1-based page numbers\n\nFixes #57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794111287.6652398, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "## Summary\n\n`catalog.pager.page()` treated `number` as 0-based, so `page(items, 1, size)` returned the second page even though the API documents page numbers as 1-based.\n\nChanged the offset calculation to `(number - 1) * size` so `?page=1` returns the first page.\n\n## Verification\n\nChecked locally:\n- `page(range(1, 11), 1, 3)` -> `[1, 2, 3]`\n- `page(range(1, 11), 2, 3)` -> `[4, 5, 6]`\n- `page(range(1, 11), 4, 3)` -> `[10]`\n- `page(range(1, 11), 5, 3)` -> `[]`\n\nFixes #57", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix 1-based pagination in page()"}, "ok": true}
